{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T13:51:02Z","input_tokens":3082,"cache_read_tokens":105851,"output_tokens":6075,"thinking":"I'm dividing work between subagents: one handles the landing/privacy pages and adult auth with parent/teacher dashboards and server actions, while I take the child login flow, mission map, mission play, block editor, Bibi API, progress API, seed data, and tests. I'm reconsidering the split since child login needs family codes that overlap with the dashboard work.\n\nI need to define clear contracts — family code generation (random 6-char unique code at registration), bcrypt-hashed PINs for children, chat logs, and activity charts pulled from attempt records. I should instruct subagents to avoid running dev servers, builds, or installs concurrently (only type-checking), noting the slow filesystem and npm.cmd/npx.cmd usage, and spell out the landing page routes and scope, skipping the optional mini-game feature since only must-haves and most should-haves were chosen.\n\nThe foundation's done. Now I'll parallelize: one subagent builds the landing page, another handles adult auth and the parent/teacher dashboard, while I build the child area—login, map, block editor, and Bibi AI.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Subagents":[{"Prompt":"You are building part of **CodeKids**, a Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4) kids coding-education web app in `e:\\codekids`. Read `e:\\codekids\\PRD.md` sections 4.1, 5.1, 5.2, 5.3 first. UI language: **Bahasa Indonesia** (simple, friendly).\n\n## Your task: Landing page + privacy page ONLY\nCreate:\n1. `e:\\codekids\\src\\app\\page.tsx` — landing page (React Server Component; only small client components where interactivity is needed, put them in `src/components/landing/`).\n   - FR-LP-01 Hero: headline, Bibi mascot illustration, two CTAs: \"Mulai Petualangan\" → `/masuk` (child login) and \"Untuk Orang Tua/Guru\" → `/akun/daftar`. Header nav with Logo + links (`#cara-belajar`, `#bibi`, `#orang-tua`) + \"Masuk\" button for adults → `/akun/masuk`.\n   - FR-LP-02 \"Cara Belajar\" section (id `cara-belajar`): 3 level cards with icon + hover animation. Import `LEVELS` from `@/content/missions` (fields: level, concept, title, subtitle, emoji, color) and mention curriculum ties (Level 1 Sequencing: siklus air, tumbuh kembang tanaman, penjumlahan bersusun; Level 2 Looping: perkalian sbg penjumlahan berulang, pola bilangan, detak jantung, fase bulan; Level 3 IF-ELSE: genap/ganjil, terapung/tenggelam, herbivora/karnivora).\n   - FR-LP-03 \"Kenalan dengan Bibi AI\" (id `bibi`): interactive demo — a client component that plays a short static chat conversation (e.g. child: \"Kenapa looping-ku nggak jalan?\" Bibi: \"Bayangkan kamu menyiram 5 pot bunga...\") with typing animation, plus 2–3 tappable quick-question chips that reveal different canned Bibi replies. Explain tiered hints (Tingkat 1 pertanyaan pemandu, 2 analogi, 3 petunjuk spesifik) and that Bibi never gives the full answer.\n   - FR-LP-04 Parents/teachers section (id `orang-tua`): a static mock/preview of the dashboard built with HTML/Tailwind (summary stats, concept mastery chips \"Sudah Paham / Sedang Belajar / Perlu Bantuan\", mini bar chart), plus safety guarantees (no child email/personal data, parental consent, AI safety filters, UU PDP compliance, no ads).\n   - FR-LP-05 Micro-interactions: floating mascot, bouncy buttons, floating decorative elements. Must respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (globals.css already disables animations under that media query — just use the provided animation utilities).\n   - FR-LP-07 Footer: links to `/privasi`, contact (e.g. halo@codekids.id), competition info (\"Dibuat untuk M-ONE Telkomsel Coding Competition, tema Web Education for Kids\").\n2. `e:\\codekids\\src\\app\\privasi\\page.tsx` — simple-language privacy policy (Kebijakan Privasi) consistent with PRD 5.4: data minimization (nickname, avatar, grade only), parental consent, Bibi AI does not store personal data and redacts it, parents can export/delete data, UU PDP Indonesia, cookies only for login session.\n\n## Existing pieces you MUST reuse (do not modify them)\n- Design tokens in `src/app/globals.css` (Tailwind v4 `@theme`): colors `peach`, `peach-200`, `peach-300`, `navy`, `navy-700`, `navy-300`, `orange`, `orange-600`, `orange-700` (use for orange TEXT on light bg for contrast), `cta`, `leaf`, `leaf-700`, `sky`, `sky-700`, `berry`, `sun`, `ink`. Fonts: `font-display` (Baloo 2, headings) and `font-sans` (Nunito). Shadows: `shadow-pop`, `shadow-pop-sm`, `shadow-soft`. Animations: `animate-float`, `animate-wiggle`, `animate-pop-in`, `animate-bounce-soft`. Utilities: `btn-primary` (orange pill CTA), `btn-navy`, `btn-ghost`, `btn-leaf`, `card`, `chip`, `input`, `label`. Read globals.css before starting.\n- `@/components/brand/BibiMascot` → `<BibiMascot mood=\"happy\"|\"thinking\"|\"cheer\" className=\"...\" />` (inline SVG).\n- `@/components/brand/Logo` → `<Logo />`.\n- Read `src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout already sets fonts and `lang=\"id\"`).\n\n## Requirements\n- Mobile-first, breakpoints 360/768/1280 px; WCAG AA contrast; touch targets ≥ 48px; semantic HTML, ARIA labels, keyboard navigable; don't rely only on color.\n- Performance: keep the page a Server Component; no new npm packages; no external images (use the SVG mascot, emoji, and CSS shapes). Export `metadata` where useful.\n- Do NOT create or edit files outside `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/privasi/`, and `src/components/landing/`. Other agents are concurrently building `/masuk`, `/peta`, `/misi`, `/akun`, `/dashboard` and API routes.\n\n## Environment notes\n- Windows + PowerShell. `npm`/`npx` are blocked by execution policy: use `npm.cmd` / `npx.cmd`. The filesystem is slow; commands can take minutes.\n- Do NOT run `npm install`, `next dev`, or `next build` (others are working concurrently). Dependencies may still be installing; when `node_modules/typescript` exists you may run `npx.cmd tsc --noEmit -p e:\\codekids` to type-check, and only care about errors in your own files.\n\nWhen done, reply with a short summary listing the files you created.","Role":"Landing Page Builder","TypeName":"self"},{"Prompt":"You are building part of **CodeKids**, a Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Prisma 6 + SQLite) kids coding-education web app in `e:\\codekids`. Read `e:\\codekids\\PRD.md` (esp. sections 4.2, 4.5, 5.1, 5.4, 6.2, 6.3) first. UI language: **Bahasa Indonesia** (adult-facing, clear and plain).\n\n## Your task: adult authentication + Parent/Teacher dashboard\nBuild with Server Components + Server Actions (use `\"use server\"` action files and `zod` for validation; `useActionState` for forms in small client components). Routes:\n1. `/akun/daftar` — register parent or teacher (role picker: \"Orang Tua\" / \"Guru\"), name, email, password (min 8). Hash with `bcryptjs` (cost 10). For PARENT generate a unique `familyCode` via `randomCode(6)` from `@/lib/codes` (retry on collision). Then `createAdultSession(user.id, role)` and redirect to `/dashboard`. (Google sign-in and email verification are out of scope for this local MVP; you can show a small note.)\n2. `/akun/masuk` — login; `/akun/keluar` logout via server action (`clearAdultSession`).\n3. `/dashboard` — adult home (protected via `requireAdult()` from `@/lib/session`).\n   - PARENT: shows the **Kode Keluarga** (familyCode) prominently with instructions: child opens `/masuk`, enters Kode Keluarga, picks their avatar, enters their 4-digit PIN. Lists children with summary cards (total stars, score, level, rank, weekly learning time). Form \"Tambah Anak\": nickname (max 20 chars), avatar picker (`AVATARS` from `@/lib/constants`), grade 1–6 (`GRADES`), REQUIRED parental-consent checkbox (FR-AUTH-05; set `consentAt`), generates a 4-digit PIN with `randomPin()` (store only `bcrypt` hash in `pinHash`) and shows the PIN ONCE after creation. Multiple children per parent (FR-AUTH-04).\n   - TEACHER: list of classes + \"Buat Kelas\" (name) generating unique `code` via `randomCode(6)`; teacher must tick a checkbox confirming they have parent/school permission.\n4. `/dashboard/anak/[id]` — child detail (access check with `adultCanAccessChild(userId, childId)` from `@/lib/session`; 404 otherwise):\n   - FR-DASH-01 summary: total stars, score, current level, rank, weekly learning time (sum of `Attempt.durationSec` in last 7 days).\n   - FR-DASH-02 per-level/per-mission table: status, stars, attempts, hints used (from `Progress`).\n   - FR-DASH-03 concept mastery for Sequencing / Looping / IF-ELSE with labels \"Sudah Paham\"/\"Sedang Belajar\"/\"Perlu Bantuan\"/\"Belum Mulai\" — use icon + text, not color only.\n   - FR-DASH-04 activity chart: last 7 days and last 4 weeks (stars earned & missions attempted), implemented as accessible SVG/CSS bars (no chart library).\n   - FR-DASH-07 Bibi chat history grouped by mission, with a simple topic summary (e.g. count of questions per mission + which hint levels were reached; flagged messages marked).\n   - FR-DASH-08 settings (parent only, or teacher for class students where sensible): daily learning limit in minutes (null = no limit; options e.g. 15/30/45/60/none), reset PIN (shows new PIN once), toggle sound, delete child data (confirm step), and NFR-SC-04 export all child data as JSON (Route Handler `src/app/api/export/anak/[id]/route.ts` with the same access check, `Content-Disposition: attachment`).\n5. `/dashboard/kelas/[id]` — teacher class view (only the owning teacher): shows class code + invite instructions (students open `/masuk`, choose \"Kode Kelas\", enter the code, then pick their name + PIN, or join as new student) (FR-DASH-06). FR-DASH-05: student table sortable (name, stars, score, last active) and filterable (search + filter \"Perlu bantuan\" / \"Tidak aktif\"), with flags: inactive = no attempt in last 7 days (or never), struggling = many failed attempts (e.g. ≥ 6 fails and fail ratio > 0.75 in last 14 days). Teacher can add a student (nickname, avatar, grade → shows generated PIN once). Each row links to `/dashboard/anak/[id]`. FR-DASH-09 export class CSV via route handler `src/app/api/export/kelas/[id]/route.ts`.\n\n## Existing code you MUST reuse (read these files first; do not modify them unless there's a real bug — tell me if so)\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` — models User(role \"PARENT\"|\"TEACHER\", familyCode), Class(code), ChildProfile(nickname, avatar, grade, pinHash, parentId, classId, consentAt, dailyLimitMin, soundOn, lastActiveAt), Progress, Attempt, ChildBadge, ChatLog.\n- `src/lib/db.ts` (`db` Prisma client), `src/lib/session.ts` (`createAdultSession`, `getAdultSession`, `requireAdult`, `clearAdultSession`, `adultCanAccessChild`), `src/lib/codes.ts` (`randomCode`, `randomPin`, `normalizeCode`), `src/lib/constants.ts` (`AVATARS`, `GRADES`).\n- `src/lib/missions/gamification.ts` — `totals(progress)`, `rankFor`, `conceptMastery(concept, progress, attempts)`, `BADGES`, `badgeById`, `starsInLevel`, `maxStarsInLevel`. `src/content/missions.ts` — `MISSIONS`, `LEVELS`, `missionsByLevel`, `getMission`.\n- Design tokens/utilities in `src/app/globals.css` (Tailwind v4): colors `peach`, `navy`, `orange`, `orange-700` (orange text), `cta`, `leaf`, `leaf-700`, `sky`, `berry`, `sun`, `ink`; utilities `btn-primary`, `btn-navy`, `btn-ghost`, `btn-leaf`, `card`, `chip`, `input`, `label`; fonts `font-display`/`font-sans`. `@/components/brand/Logo`, `@/components/brand/BibiMascot`.\n- Next.js 16 notes: `params` and `searchParams` are Promises (`const { id } = await params`), `cookies()` is async. Don't use middleware/proxy; protect each page server-side.\n\n## Requirements\n- Dashboard must be visually separated from the kids area (NFR-UX-07): put a shared layout at `src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx` with a calmer adult header (Logo, user name, role badge, logout). Put auth pages under `src/app/akun/`.\n- RBAC everywhere (NFR-SC-03): every server action re-checks session + ownership. Never trust IDs from the client.\n- Responsive, accessible (labels, ARIA, keyboard), WCAG AA contrast.\n- Put reusable dashboard components in `src/components/dashboard/` and server actions in `src/app/akun/actions.ts` and `src/app/dashboard/actions.ts`. Data-loading helpers may go in `src/lib/dashboard.ts`.\n- Do NOT create/edit files outside: `src/app/akun/**`, `src/app/dashboard/**`, `src/app/api/export/**`, `src/components/dashboard/**`, `src/lib/dashboard.ts`. Other agents are concurrently building `/` (landing), `/masuk`, `/peta`, `/misi` and `/api/bibi`, `/api/progress`.\n\n## Environment notes\n- Windows + PowerShell. `npm`/`npx` are blocked by execution policy: use `npm.cmd` / `npx.cmd`. Filesystem is slow; commands may take minutes.\n- Do NOT run `npm install`, `next dev`, `next build`, or Prisma migrations (I will run them). Dependencies may still be installing; once `node_modules/typescript` and `node_modules/.prisma/client` exist you may run `npx.cmd tsc --noEmit -p e:\\codekids` and only fix errors in your own files. If `@prisma/client` types are not generated yet, you may run `npx.cmd prisma generate` once.\n\nWhen done, reply with a concise summary of routes/files created and anything I need to know.","Role":"Dashboard & Auth Builder","TypeName":"self"}],"toolAction":"Launching parallel builders","toolSummary":"Parallel subagents"}}]}
